{"ts":"2026-07-25T12:30:36.097Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-g608fc"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Domain-pack authoring kit: the reusable substrate for modeling a foreign domain — types, typed edges, invariants, projections, lifecycle — with a scaffold that proves it end to end"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Two exemplars have proven the universal claim by construction: a minimal custom PM tool and a temporal digital-twin graph. Both were built by hand against SDK primitives, and neither left behind reusable substrate. The next author of a foreign domain repeats the same discovery work — which primitive models an entity, how to declare custom types and statuses, how to express an invariant that the engine will enforce rather than merely document, how to define a projection that stays bounded, how to attach domain lifecycle rules without forking the lifecycle engine. Package that path: a domain-pack shape with declared types, declared edge kinds and their semantics, declared invariants checked by validation, declared projections honoring the token budget, and declared lifecycle rules — plus a scaffold that generates a working pack and a conformance test that tells an author whether their pack is correct. The kit is also the honest test of the SDK boundary: every gap an author would hit is a missing SDK primitive, and finding those gaps is half the value of building it."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:sdk","customization","extensibility","platform","universal-domain"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-25T12:30:36.097Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-25T12:30:36.097Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":720},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A domain pack declares custom types, custom edge kinds with their semantics, invariants, projections, and lifecycle rules through documented public SDK surface only, with no private core imports; Declared invariants are enforced by validation, so a pack can make an illegal state unrepresentable rather than merely discouraged; Declared projections honor the token budget and degrade deterministically, like core read surfaces; A scaffold generates a working pack, and a conformance test tells an author whether their pack is correct, with named failures rather than a generic error; Building the kit produces a filed item for every SDK gap encountered, linked to this item as discovered_from, and none are worked around privately; The kit is exercised by rebuilding at least one existing exemplar on top of it, proving it is sufficient rather than merely plausible"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Modeling a foreign domain on pm is a declared pack, not a from-scratch integration project"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"The universal-platform milestone is unreachable while each domain is bespoke; a kit is what turns two proofs of concept into a repeatable capability"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"Formalizes the extension surface a domain author depends on, which raises the compatibility bar for that surface; gaps found while building it become SDK promotion work"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"A developer models a new domain in hours using declared substrate, and every gap they hit is a filed SDK primitive rather than a workaround"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-8jdc"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":60},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-8jdc","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:30:36.097Z"},{"id":"pm-8ngt","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:30:36.097Z"},{"id":"pm-cbwg","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:30:36.097Z"},{"id":"pm-e1va","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:30:36.097Z"},{"id":"pm-ju83","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:30:36.097Z"},{"id":"pm-kr3t","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:30:36.097Z"},{"id":"pm-t4d7nz","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:30:36.097Z"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"78252fc7abfc2a552a7112c377ccfd165cf9eed4a6a55c2e8088b839dd85e6e5","message":"File the reusable substrate that turns one-off domain exemplars into a repeatable capability"}
